  "chapter": {
    "bookTitle": "Job",
    "delineation": "Chapter",
    "number": 37,
    "summary": "Elihu concludes, saying, The Lord controls the laws of nature—God reigns in terrible majesty.",
    "chapterAugmentations": [],
    "verses": [
      {
        "text": "At this also my heart trembleth, and is moved out of his place.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 1,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 37:1",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 37,
        "verse": 1
      },
      {
        "text": "Hear attentively the noise of his voice, and the sound that goeth out of his mouth.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 55,
            "end": 59
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 2,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 37:2",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 37,
        "verse": 2
      },
      {
        "text": "He directeth it under the whole heaven, and his lightning unto the ends of the earth.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 3,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 37:3",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 37,
        "verse": 3
      },
      {
        "text": "After it a voice roareth: he thundereth with the voice of his excellency; and he will not stay them when his voice is heard.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 4,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 37:4",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 37,
        "verse": 4
      },
      {
        "text": "God thundereth marvellously with his voice; great things doeth he, which we cannot comprehend.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 5,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 37:5",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 37,
        "verse": 5
      },
      {
        "text": "For he saith to the snow, Be thou on the earth; likewise to the small rain, and to the great rain of his strength.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 20,
            "end": 24,
            "text": "TG Nature, Earth."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 34,
            "end": 36
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 6,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "TG Nature, Earth.",
            "prettyString": "TG Nature, Earth",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "studyHelp",
                "studyHelpType": "tg",
                "title": "Nature, Earth",
                "entryId": "tg-nature-earth",
                "book": "",
                "chapters": []
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 37:6",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 37,
        "verse": 6
      },
      {
        "text": "He sealeth up the hand of every man; that all men may know his work.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 7,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 37:7",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 37,
        "verse": 7
      },
      {
        "text": "Then the beasts go into dens, and remain in their places.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 8,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 37:8",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 37,
        "verse": 8
      },
      {
        "text": "Out of the south cometh the whirlwind: and cold out of the north.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 9,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 37:9",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 37,
        "verse": 9
      },
      {
        "text": "By the breath of God frost is given: and the breadth of the waters is straitened.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 10,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 37:10",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 37,
        "verse": 10
      },
      {
        "text": "Also by watering he wearieth the thick cloud: he scattereth his bright cloud:",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 11,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 37:11",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 37,
        "verse": 11
      },
      {
        "text": "And it is turned round about by his counsels: that they may do whatsoever he commandeth them upon the face of the world in the earth.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 12,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 37:12",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 37,
        "verse": 12
      },
      {
        "text": "He causeth it to come, whether for correction, or for his land, or for mercy.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 13,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 37:13",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 37,
        "verse": 13
      },
      {
