        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 37:16",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 37,
        "verse": 16
      },
      {
        "text": "How thy garments are warm, when he quieteth the earth by the south wind?",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 17,
            "end": 20
          },
          {
            "start": 67,
            "end": 72
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 17,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 37:17",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 37,
        "verse": 17
      },
      {
        "text": "Hast thou with him spread out the sky, which is strong, and as a molten looking glass?",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 39,
            "end": 47
          },
          {
            "start": 56,
            "end": 59
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 18,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 37:18",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 37,
        "verse": 18
      },
      {
        "text": "Teach us what we shall say unto him; for we cannot order our speech by reason of darkness.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 37,
            "end": 40
          },
          {
            "start": 57,
            "end": 67
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 19,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 37:19",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 37,
        "verse": 19
      },
      {
        "text": "Shall it be told him that I speak? if a man speak, surely he shall be swallowed up.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 20,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 37:20",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 37,
        "verse": 20
      },
      {
        "text": "And now men see not the bright light which is in the clouds: but the wind passeth, and cleanseth them.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 8,
            "end": 11
          },
          {
            "start": 43,
            "end": 45
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 21,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 37:21",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 37,
        "verse": 21
      },
      {
        "text": "Fair weather cometh out of the north: with God is terrible majesty.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 47,
            "end": 49
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 22,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 37:22",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 37,
        "verse": 22
      },
      {
